`sysmon` EventCode=10 TargetImage="*\\lsass.exe"
    (GrantedAccess=0x1010 OR GrantedAccess=0x1410 OR GrantedAccess=0x1438 OR GrantedAccess=0x1FFFFF)
    NOT SourceImage IN ("C:\\Windows\\System32\\*", "C:\\Program Files\\*", "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\*")
| stats count min(_time) as first_seen max(_time) as last_seen values(SourceImage) as tools by ComputerName
| where count > 0
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)

```
LSASS Memory Access Detection
Author: fungiknight (Gabriel Lopez)
MITRE: T1003.001 (OS Credential Dumping: LSASS Memory)

Detects processes accessing LSASS memory with suspicious
GrantedAccess values commonly used by credential-dumping tools
(Mimikatz, comsvcs.dll MiniDump, procdump).

Filters:
  - Excludes System32/Program Files (legitimate AV and OS processes)
  - GrantedAccess 0x1010 = PROCESS_QUERY_LIMITED_INFORMATION + PROCESS_VM_READ
  - GrantedAccess 0x1FFFFF = PROCESS_ALL_ACCESS (most suspicious)
```
